'docs/PRD.md': '''# Product requirements

## Product

greenfield-proof is a small TypeScript reusable greeting API plus CLI for developers. The public behavior is specified in [UX canon](ux-canon.md).

## Audience

Developers importing a typed greeting function and invoking its CLI.

## Platforms

Node 22+ on Linux; the cached generator requires Node 22.12 or later on the selected runtime line.

## Constraints

Use npm, TypeScript, tsup and node:test. Private UNLICENSED fixture; no publishing or fixture commits. Adapt the cached create-vite 8.3.0 vanilla-ts scaffold directly in this repository. Preserve any present home byte-identically; stop if unexpected homes appear.

## Non-goals

No framework runtime, external service, HTTP backend, authentication, mobile application, deployment, product remote or publishing. This API is an imported function, not a network service.

## Success signals

Meaningful API and CLI tests, typecheck, build, built CLI smoke, catalog comparison, roadmap config check, actual emission and the complete installed delivery validation suite pass. Simulation success does not imply a hosted CI run or deployment. A separate read-only brownfield re-audit follows execution.

## Brand

Non-Blade. No graphical UI. Registry absent/none because there are no UI components; no invented tokens, fonts or palette.

