'docs/ux-canon.md': '''# UX canon

## Visual language

Plain terminal text. Fonts, palette, spacing and visual tokens are inapplicable.

## Component vocabulary

An imported greet(name?: string) function and the greenfield-proof CLI. No graphical components or registry.

## Interaction rules

greet() and greet(undefined) return Hello, world!. A supplied nonblank string returns Hello, <name>! with its characters preserved. Empty or whitespace-only names throw TypeError; nonstring JavaScript inputs also throw TypeError.

The CLI accepts zero or one name and prints the greeting plus a newline to stdout. The sole --help argument prints usage to stdout and exits 0. Unknown options, extra arguments and blank names print an error and usage to stderr, print no greeting, and exit 1. Successful greetings exit 0. Usage is:

    Usage: greenfield-proof [name]
           greenfield-proof --help

## Binding design system

None, as ruled in [ADR 0002](adr/0002-design-system.md). Non-Blade; registry absent/none because there is no UI. Do not introduce visual tokens without a new approved requirement.
''',
