## Conventions

Keep reusable behavior in src/index.ts and process I/O in src/cli.ts. Use strict TypeScript and node:test with node:assert/strict. Exercise CLI behavior through real subprocesses. README owns runnable command guidance; roadmap/roadmap.config.json owns gate bindings. Product, architecture and UX facts remain in their linked independent docs homes.

## Don't

Do not introduce a framework runtime, external service, authentication, mobile UI, product remote, publishing or deployment. Do not invent design tokens or duplicate conventions into harness files. Do not assume plugin-internal paths in consumer code. Do not commit inside this native fixture.

## Generalize-forward

Extract a shared abstraction when a second real consumer needs the same behavior; preserve the small API/process boundary until then.

