'README.md': '''# greenfield-proof

A private TypeScript greeting API and CLI for developers. See [product requirements](docs/PRD.md) and the [CLI contract](docs/ux-canon.md).

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| src/index.ts | Reusable greeting API |
| src/cli.ts | Executable process adapter |
| test/ | API and real CLI subprocess tests |
| tsup.config.ts | ESM build and declarations |
| dist/ | Built API and CLI outputs |
| docs/ | Product, ADR, standards, architecture and UX homes |
| roadmap/ | Vendored roadmap tooling, config, phases and arcs |
| reviews/ | Emitted changelog and release review home |
| scripts/ | Copied catalog, delivery and review tooling |
| .github/greenfield-delivery.json | Complete delivery execution contract |
| .github/workflows/ci.yml | Affected/local/full test lifecycle and authoritative backstop |
| .github/workflows/release.yml | Exact-artifact release verification; promotion unavailable |

## Commands

Use Node 22.12+ on Linux. npm commands use npm_config_cache=$PWD/.npm-cache and npm_config_logs_dir=$PWD/.npm-logs so caches stay local.

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| npm ci --no-audit --no-fund | Install the retained lockfile |
| npm run typecheck | Check source, build config and roadmap types |
| npm test | Full local API and CLI behavior suite |
| npm run build | Build dist with tsup |
| node dist/cli.js --help | Built CLI smoke check |
| npm run emit:phases | Emit reviews/changelog.json |
| npm run changelog:md | Optional later Markdown changelog generation |
| node scripts/ci-shard-plan.mjs affected | PR checks; requires the real BASE_SHA and deliberately runs full tests |

The installed catalog checker is scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs, bound to project-root mode with source dot and project name greenfield-proof. Lint and browser e2e are explicitly absent; they are not passing gates.

## Delivery

.github/workflows/ci.yml runs the full small suite for PRs because no dependency-aware selector exists. Main and manual runs inventory real tracked test files, shard exactly once, merge actual JUnit and LCOV, build once and produce authoritative evidence. Nightly runs diagnose without authoritative release evidence. The backstop is .github/workflows/ci.yml (authoritative full suite on main/manual runs).

.github/workflows/release.yml verifies the exact previously built artifact. The protected environment is greenfield-validation. Deployment provider none is explicitly unavailable; no publish or deployment is authorized. Baseline: 10 tests, 2 units, 80 percent line coverage; two requested shards. Evidence retention is seven days, raw diagnostics three days, verified promotion one day. Canonical workflows retain their immutable action pins and least-privilege jobs.

The native fixture does not commit or run a hosted workflow. Installed workflow simulations are validation evidence, not a live GitHub run. A separate read-only brownfield audit follows approved execution.

